--TEST--
A key only one arm of `Db\Settings` requires is required of the call that selects that arm, asked of both arms — `rule:core-api/shape-arms-are-disjoint`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// The half of § 2 that the merged list understates rather than overstates. A
// key is required of the *merged* parameter only where every arm requires it,
// which for `Db\Settings` is `driver` alone — so before arm selection a server
// literal could omit `user` and a SQLite literal could omit `path`, and the
// helper would read a slot § 3 promises is filled.
var $server = Core\Db::open({
    driver: Core\Db\Driver::Postgres,
    host: "db.example.test",
    database: "shop",
    password: "hunter2",
});

// Both arms, because a rule written for one of them reads the same on the line
// that has it and refuses nothing on the line that does not: the SQLite arm
// requires `path`, and the arm this literal selects is the one its `driver`
// value names.
var $file = Core\Db::open({
    driver: Core\Db\Driver::Sqlite,
});
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0402]: this member requires the shape key `user`
%A
error[E0402]: this member requires the shape key `path`
%A
error: aborting due to 2 errors
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
